  "body": "## Scope / dependency\n\nDepends on #380 (`codex/payment-closed-checkout-evidence-20260915`) and the documented payment stack. Companion mobile draft: https://github.com/diegueins680/TDF-mobile/pull/82 (after mobile #81).\n\n- Append strict-admin GET `/admin/commerce/reconciliation-exceptions`: sandbox default, validated bounded filters, read-only SQL, three-second statement timeout, no-store, explicit schema readiness and redacted failures.\n- Return allowlisted classifications, nullable exact signed-64-bit minor-unit strings and internal links only for a unique matching stored binding. No merchant aliases, external provider references, payloads, notes, assignment identities or lookup tokens.\n- Add responsive Spanish/English web admin panel with safe filter/refresh/pagination, exact BigInt USD formatting, explicit non-USD minor units, stale/mismatched-response hiding and neutral review labels.\n- Regenerate both API clients; pin mobile `33720ef45b0565005c4b54b0e0c106cc93831613`. No native admin screen.\n- Document ADR 0125, threat boundaries, operator procedure, rollback, failed attempts and successful local verification.\n\nRead-only means no provider contact, query-budget reservation, charge, refund, hold release, settlement or payout. Resolved/ignored review labels do not release a held payment. This is operational evidence, not a booked-cash ledger or immutable accounting export.\n\n## Verification \u2014 local 2026-09-15 UTC\n\nFrozen runtime source: `174847ab441e0cca0724259f989294fdd0ae4095`; later changes documentation only. Backend source is frozen since `af97d31927e1ebbf9eaf4ab29049216d29dcbd40`.\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `stack test --fast --rerun-tests` | 2599 examples, 0 failures; 17:40:49 UTC log completion. |\n| `TDF_PROVIDER_RETRY_DATABASE_URL=<isolated local Unix socket> sh scripts/test-provider-retry-runtime.sh` | 206 examples, 0 failures; 17:38:10 UTC. Includes 13 migration dependencies, repeat apply, empty rollback/operator seed retention, reapply and populated-history rollback refusal. |\n| Four targeted web suites | 40 tests, 0 failures; 17:18:45 UTC. |\n| Three targeted mobile payment suites | 13 tests, 0 failures; 17:20:50 UTC. |\n| Web/mobile typecheck; changed-file ESLint | Passed, no relaxed warning threshold. |\n| Web production build / initial-bundle budget | Passed; five preloads, 314065 gzip bytes. Existing large-chunk warning remains. |\n| `npm run quality:repo` | 160 tests, 0 failures, repeated at 17:41:20 UTC. Formal scan has 377 existing warnings; no certification claimed. |\n| Catalog authority audit | 1424 files, 1131 candidates, 0 unreviewed, 0 stale; 17:34:06.799 UTC. Three explicit new redaction/filter review entries; gate unchanged. |\n| Generated web/mobile comparison; diff whitespace; new-doc relative links | Passed. |\n| Offline Metro startup / localhost status | Passed with approved socket access, dotenv and remote Expo services disabled; stopped afterward. No device checkout claimed. |\n\nAll provider evidence/accounts/amounts are synthetic. These are mocked/local and real-local-PostgreSQL tests, **not provider sandbox tests**. Exact commands, local log paths, SHAs, timestamps and initial failures (socket restriction, missing test import, nonempty DB refusal, Metro argument/port errors) are in `docs/payments/reconciliation-evidence-2026-09-15.md`. Both temporary database clusters and Metro were stopped; evidence retained, no material data deleted.\n\n## Migration / rollout / rollback\n\nNo migration, backfill, new index, historical-data rewrite, secret or feature activation. Deploy backend reader before web; older backend fails unavailable, not empty-success. Removing this additive reader/view does not remove evidence; **retain #380's held-payment behavior**, never delete an exception to recover a redirect. Live offset pages may shift and production-volume performance is unverified.\n\nMerge order: root stack through #380; mobile #81 then #82; this reader/UI PR with the pinned mobile SHA. Preserve main's unrelated changes and mobile #80's social-contract additions when eventually reconciling lineages. No merge or formal review request performed here.\n\n## Blockers / unexecuted\n\nLast authorized staging inspector evidence remains 2026-09-15T16:14:06.284Z: healthy public staging endpoints but unavailable hosting authentication, unknown source SHA, providerQualified=false. Restore approved `FLY_STAGING_API_TOKEN` / `FLY_STAGING_WEB_TOKEN` access or authorized Fly login; qualify deployed SHA, sandbox merchant aliases/contracts/secret names and webhook registration.\n\nNo new provider sandbox, staging deployment/transaction, production deployment, live charge, refund or payout. No screenshot, native build, simulator/device manual QA or full-web-suite claim. Approved financial remediation/hold release, recurring/saved methods, settlement/seller-payout workflows, legacy Datafast/PayPal late-observation handling and qualified Ecuadorian legal/accounting/PCI review remain separate incomplete work. This is a bounded completed increment, not payment-platform completion.\n",
